# WingSim-Faders.ReaperOSC: REAPER OSC pattern config for the Wing Simulator (T065).
#
# Everything in WingSim-Markers.ReaperOSC, plus REAPER tracks 1-40 drive WING channels 1-40:
#   track volume (dB, including volume automation)  -> /ch/N/fdr ,f <dB>  (clamped to -144..+10)
#   track mute (including mute automation)          -> /ch/N/mute ,f 0|1
# REAPER sends these as control-surface feedback, so there is no per-message process spawn and
# automation playback reaches the simulator at the surface update rate.
#
# Limits: one-way (fader moves on the simulator do not move REAPER); REAPER sends the current
# value of every mapped track when the surface starts or the project changes, which overrides
# the simulator's faders/mutes for those channels (including right after a scene recall).
# Track N maps to channel N by position, not by name. Pan/EQ/sends are not mapped.

DEVICE_TRACK_COUNT 40
DEVICE_SEND_COUNT 0
DEVICE_RECEIVE_COUNT 0
DEVICE_FX_COUNT 0
DEVICE_FX_PARAM_COUNT 0
DEVICE_FX_INST_PARAM_COUNT 0
DEVICE_MARKER_COUNT 0
DEVICE_REGION_COUNT 0

LAST_MARKER_NAME s/wingsim/marker
LAST_REGION_NAME s/wingsim/region

TRACK_VOLUME f/ch/@/fdr
TRACK_MUTE b/ch/@/mute
